Task: Frame sampler (Phase 2, Track foundation-core_20260918)

Red phase: tests written first, failed on the missing module. Green phase: ten
new tests pass, eighteen in total.

What the tests pin down:
- The requested number of moving frames is produced, and held beats add to that
  total rather than replacing moving frames.
- The first and last positions are exact, which matters because a motion that
  lands slightly short looks broken.
- Held beats repeat the extreme positions instead of inventing new ones.
- Progress never moves backwards.
- A held beat can last longer than a moving one, and every frame carries a
  positive duration.
- A curve can be passed by name or as a function, so presets can carry a name
  as plain data.
- Fewer than two frames and a negative hold count are both rejected with a
  message that says what is wrong.

Design notes:
- Defaults are named constants rather than inline numbers, since frame duration
  and hold length are exactly the kind of tunable the style guide says belongs
  in data.
- Each frame records whether it is held, which the later layers need in order
  to know where a pose is deliberately frozen.
